{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":67485,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"8e7ca88a08b62dad30462b3a15b7e1ba","RawContent":"[quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]alexisinjamaica[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n I am kind of all over the place with colors. I waffle between wanting fun, bright, summery colors like lemon yellow and lime green and turquoise, and more muted tones like purples, creams and greys because that&#039;s more me. I feel like I should go bright since it&#039;ll be springtime, on the beach and in Jamaica, but I keep finding myself drawn to purple things. Like this bouquet (it&#039;s actually paper!!) that I saw in an Etsy shop. \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/155334\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img][\/quote] \n Maybe try keeping the colors something that&#039;s at least a little you so that the wedding reflects some of your style.  The colors in the bouquet are awesome together.  I really can&#039;t believe that&#039;s paper either.. amazing!   \n \n You could do a little of both, a little bright and fun and a little of you.  I like neutral colors so I chose originally I wanted black and white with [i]maybe [\/i]an accent color.  The more I thought about it, though, the more I disliked that color scheme for a beach wedding.  So, I went to look at paint samples in a store - I know that sounds silly, but it was really nice to be able to put the colors together to see how they complimented each other.  After about ten minutes I decided I wanted coral and dark grey.  I really wanted at least one bright color to stand out against the ocean (we&#039;re getting married on the beach in Mexico)  but I didn&#039;t want to do have all bright colors because that just isn&#039;t my style, so I chose a comfort color.  I&#039;m really happy with choice.  I&#039;ve also stopped thinking about it; I chose my colors and I&#039;m done. :)  So maybe something to keep in mind, that you can have the best of both.    The more I look at the picture of the flowers above, the more I LOVE those colors together... and I&#039;m not a fan of purple. :) \n \n My girlfriend did onyx, pewter and aqua-ish color.  It looked amazing, and really classy.   Here&#039;s one that has some colors you might like as a starting point since you like purples and greys (bourdeax, wisteria and silver):  \n \n [img]http:\/\/scmedia.theknot.com\/~\/media\/808D1D333E2C45258730EE53B2B267D6.ashx[\/img]","Attachments":[],"Id":1648759,"PostDate":1343983506,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>alexisinjamaica<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> I am kind of all over the place with colors. I waffle between wanting fun, bright, summery colors like lemon yellow and lime green and turquoise, and more muted tones like purples, creams and greys because that's more me. I feel like I should go bright since it'll be springtime, on the beach and in Jamaica, but I keep finding myself drawn to purple things. Like this bouquet (it's actually paper!!) that I saw in an Etsy shop.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p id=\"yui_3_4_1_1_1343933660086_1494\"> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' data-id=\"155334\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/155334\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <\/blockquote> <p> Maybe try keeping the colors something that's at least a little you so that the wedding reflects some of your style. \u00a0The colors in the bouquet are awesome together. \u00a0I really can't believe that's paper either.. amazing! \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> You could do a little of both, a little bright and fun and a little of you. \u00a0I like neutral colors so I chose originally I wanted black and white with <em>maybe\u00a0<\/em>an accent color. \u00a0The more I thought about it, though, the more I disliked that color scheme for a beach wedding. \u00a0So, I went to look at paint samples in a store - I know that sounds silly, but it was really nice to be able to put the colors together to see how they complimented each other. \u00a0After about ten minutes I decided I wanted\u00a0coral and dark grey. \u00a0I really wanted at least one bright color to stand out against the ocean (we're getting married on the beach in Mexico) \u00a0but I didn't want to do have all bright colors because that just isn't my style, so I chose a comfort color. \u00a0I'm really happy with choice. \u00a0I've also stopped thinking about it; I chose my colors and I'm done. <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> \u00a0So maybe something to keep in mind, that you can have the best of both. \u00a0 \u00a0The more I look at the picture of the flowers above, the more I LOVE those colors together... and I'm not a fan of purple. <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> My girlfriend did onyx, pewter and aqua-ish color. \u00a0It looked amazing, and really classy. \u00a0 Here's one that has some colors you might like as a starting point since you like purples and greys (bourdeax, wisteria and silver):\u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/scmedia.theknot.com\/~\/media\/808D1D333E2C45258730EE53B2B267D6.ashx\" \/><\/span><\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"bmelko@ymail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":47,"GroupName":"Site Supporter","JoinDate":1337785216,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-255751.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":173,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"bmelko","Id":255751,"Name":"bmelko","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":67485,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"6ec12a788b1c64feb5e03cdca962062b","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; I am debating on Black and Pink and Hot Pink and Lime Green. I think the pink and green will look better in pictures but cant decide.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; thoughts???&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1649120,"PostDate":1344073181,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> I am debating on Black and Pink and Hot Pink and Lime Green. I think the pink and green will look better in pictures but cant decide.\u00a0<\/p> <p> thoughts???\u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"a_fleetwood6@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1333230068,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-253433.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Noxx","Id":253433,"Name":"Noxx","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":67485,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"1a23124379fef2928ddf380aa988eecb","RawContent":"[quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]bmelko[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n Maybe try keeping the colors something that&#039;s at least a little you so that the wedding reflects some of your style.  The colors in the bouquet are awesome together.  I really can&#039;t believe that&#039;s paper either.. amazing!   \n \n You could do a little of both, a little bright and fun and a little of you.  I like neutral colors so I chose originally I wanted black and white with [i]maybe [\/i]an accent color.  The more I thought about it, though, the more I disliked that color scheme for a beach wedding.  So, I went to look at paint samples in a store - I know that sounds silly, but it was really nice to be able to put the colors together to see how they complimented each other.  After about ten minutes I decided I wanted coral and dark grey.  I really wanted at least one bright color to stand out against the ocean (we&#039;re getting married on the beach in Mexico)  but I didn&#039;t want to do have all bright colors because that just isn&#039;t my style, so I chose a comfort color.  I&#039;m really happy with choice.  I&#039;ve also stopped thinking about it; I chose my colors and I&#039;m done. :)  So maybe something to keep in mind, that you can have the best of both.    The more I look at the picture of the flowers above, the more I LOVE those colors together... and I&#039;m not a fan of purple. :) \n \n My girlfriend did onyx, pewter and aqua-ish color.  It looked amazing, and really classy.   Here&#039;s one that has some colors you might like as a starting point since you like purples and greys (bourdeax, wisteria and silver):  \n \n [img]http:\/\/scmedia.theknot.com\/~\/media\/808D1D333E2C45258730EE53B2B267D6.ashx[\/img][\/quote] \n \n I love everything about this. THANK YOU! Totally just saved a copy of this image for my inspiration board folder. :)","Attachments":[],"Id":1649185,"PostDate":1344101311,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>bmelko<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> Maybe try keeping the colors something that's at least a little you so that the wedding reflects some of your style. \u00a0The colors in the bouquet are awesome together. \u00a0I really can't believe that's paper either.. amazing! \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> You could do a little of both, a little bright and fun and a little of you. \u00a0I like neutral colors so I chose originally I wanted black and white with <em>maybe\u00a0<\/em>an accent color. \u00a0The more I thought about it, though, the more I disliked that color scheme for a beach wedding. \u00a0So, I went to look at paint samples in a store - I know that sounds silly, but it was really nice to be able to put the colors together to see how they complimented each other. \u00a0After about ten minutes I decided I wanted\u00a0coral and dark grey. \u00a0I really wanted at least one bright color to stand out against the ocean (we're getting married on the beach in Mexico) \u00a0but I didn't want to do have all bright colors because that just isn't my style, so I chose a comfort color. \u00a0I'm really happy with choice. \u00a0I've also stopped thinking about it; I chose my colors and I'm done. <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> \u00a0So maybe something to keep in mind, that you can have the best of both. \u00a0 \u00a0The more I look at the picture of the flowers above, the more I LOVE those colors together... and I'm not a fan of purple. <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> My girlfriend did onyx, pewter and aqua-ish color. \u00a0It looked amazing, and really classy. \u00a0 Here's one that has some colors you might like as a starting point since you like purples and greys (bourdeax, wisteria and silver):\u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/scmedia.theknot.com\/~\/media\/808D1D333E2C45258730EE53B2B267D6.ashx\" \/><\/span><\/p> <\/blockquote> <p> <br \/> I love everything about this. THANK YOU! Totally just saved a copy of this image for my inspiration board folder. <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"alexismmoore@gmail.com","IpAddress":"108.231.22.147","GroupId":38,"GroupName":"Moderators","JoinDate":1337115561,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-255437.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":667,"PhotoHeight":1000,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"alexisinjamaica","Id":255437,"Name":"alexisinjamaica","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":67485,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"2d3c1870592b4bad39564a99952e6f8e","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; hey..im having champagne bridesmaid dresses and my dress is ivory so im looking for a colour which will compliment these but having trouble...any ideas girls ? x&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1649228,"PostDate":1344147178,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> hey..im having champagne bridesmaid dresses and my dress is ivory so im looking for a colour which will compliment these but having trouble...any ideas girls ? x<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"rcandyman1@aol.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1330074783,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-251871.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":267,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"jackie44","Id":251871,"Name":"jackie44","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":67485,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"5000e5e1c35fa52146118041df70ed0b","RawContent":"[quote name=\"jackie44\"]\nhey..im having champagne bridesmaid dresses and my dress is ivory so im looking for a colour which will compliment these but having trouble...any ideas girls ? x[\/quote] What are your favorite colors?","Attachments":[],"Id":1649235,"PostDate":1344152460,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <blockquote class='ipsBlockquote' data-author=\"jackie44\" url=\"\/t\/79753\/wedding&#045;colors\/70#post_1798796\"><p>hey..im having champagne bridesmaid dresses and my dress is ivory so im looking for a colour which will compliment these but having trouble...any ideas girls ? x<\/p><\/blockquote> What are your favorite colors?\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">\"ever thine ever mine ever ours\"<\/span><span>~ Ludwig von Beethoven, and more famously by Mr. Big!<\/span><\/p><span><\/span><p><em>Now Larimar 8\/9\/13; I married my best friend! 29 of my closest friends and family celebrated with us! Couldn't have wished for anything better <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/em><\/p><span><\/span><\/div><\/div>","Email":"jam080913@gmail.com","IpAddress":"65.78.110.90","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1341004105,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-257293.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":133,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"jennifer8913","Id":257293,"Name":"jennifer8913","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":67485,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"de24ecc7a5804d9c53ebb194bee456ea","RawContent":"[quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]jackie44[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n hey..im having champagne bridesmaid dresses and my dress is ivory so im looking for a colour which will compliment these but having trouble...any ideas girls ? x[\/quote] \n \n Hi Jackie! \n \n Are you looking for an additional colour for decorations and flowers?  Are the dresses a light champaign (like a nude) or darker?   \n \n I don&#039;t think you necessarily need an additional colour ... I&#039;ve seen lots of pictures with white flowers, etc.  But if your heart is set on it I would do a shade of blue depending on the shade of champaign.  You could do a royal blue or a light aqua blue, which will look stunning with the beach and ocean. \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/155680\/width\/200\/height\/400[\/img]","Attachments":[],"Id":1649241,"PostDate":1344154402,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>jackie44<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> hey..im having champagne bridesmaid dresses and my dress is ivory so im looking for a colour which will compliment these but having trouble...any ideas girls ? x<\/p> <\/blockquote> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Hi Jackie!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Are you looking for an additional colour for decorations and flowers? \u00a0Are the dresses a light champaign (like a nude) or darker? \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I don't think you necessarily need an additional colour ... I've seen lots of pictures with white flowers, etc. \u00a0But if your heart is set on it I would do a shade of blue depending on the shade of champaign. \u00a0You could do a royal blue or a light aqua blue, which will look stunning with the beach and ocean.<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' data-id=\"155680\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/155680\/width\/200\/height\/400\" \/><\/span><\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"bridemichelle@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1335696812,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-254695.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"PuntaBride","Id":254695,"Name":"PuntaBride","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":67485,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"ea84fbbcb111dd79cc66fd5752e54bce","RawContent":"[quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]jackie44[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n hey..im having champagne bridesmaid dresses and my dress is ivory so I&#039;m looking for a colour which will compliment these but having trouble...any ideas girls ? x[\/quote] \n I have to agree with puntabride, aqua and champagne looks beautiful together. Another color that would look nice is Victorian pink.  \n \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/155771\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/155772\/width\/500\/height\/1000[\/img]","Attachments":[],"Id":1649550,"PostDate":1344248013,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>jackie44<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> hey..im having champagne bridesmaid dresses and my dress is ivory so I'm looking for a colour which will compliment these but having trouble...any ideas girls ? x<\/p> <\/blockquote> <p> I have to agree with puntabride, aqua and champagne looks beautiful together. Another color that would look nice is Victorian pink.\u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p id=\"yui_3_4_1_1_1344265662598_1642\"> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' data-id=\"155771\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/155771\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p id=\"yui_3_4_1_1_1344265662598_2349\"> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' data-id=\"155772\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/155772\/width\/500\/height\/1000\" \/><\/span><\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><\/div><\/div>","Email":"sha4966@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":47,"GroupName":"Site Supporter","JoinDate":1312894978,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-243584.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Shay4966","Id":243584,"Name":"Shay4966","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":67485,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"86ec12fa69cd4825047c8c96c17a6158","RawContent":"[quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]jackie44[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n hey..im having champagne bridesmaid dresses and my dress is ivory so im looking for a colour which will compliment these but having trouble...any ideas girls ? x[\/quote] \n \n In agreement with Shay, a blush pink or something would look nice.  If you wanted something to stand out a little more, you could try a mint-colored green, a shade of bronze, or any blue or green would work.  Even a hot color like fuchsia would look good.  It all depends on what color palette you like in your own style.  Try incorporating a color you really like by varying the shade until you find the one.   \n \n I always tells girls to go to the paint aisle in a store and grab an ivory swatch and match it to various colors until you find one you like to compliment the champagne.. people may think it&#039;s crazy, but it&#039;s very helpful. :)   \n \n Good luck!","Attachments":[],"Id":1649598,"PostDate":1344254234,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>jackie44<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> hey..im having champagne bridesmaid dresses and my dress is ivory so im looking for a colour which will compliment these but having trouble...any ideas girls ? x<\/p> <\/blockquote> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> In agreement with Shay, a blush pink or something would look nice. \u00a0If you wanted something to stand out a little more, you could try a mint-colored green, a shade of bronze, or any blue or green would work. \u00a0Even a hot color like fuchsia would look good. \u00a0It all depends on what color palette you like in your own style. \u00a0Try incorporating a color you really like by varying the shade until you find the one. \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I always tells girls to go to the paint aisle in a store and grab an ivory swatch and match it to various colors until you find one you like to compliment the champagne.. people may think it's crazy, but it's very helpful. <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Good luck!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"bmelko@ymail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":47,"GroupName":"Site Supporter","JoinDate":1337785216,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-255751.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":173,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"bmelko","Id":255751,"Name":"bmelko","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":67485,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"7944373289cfc934bc374b79c9c6d0ae","RawContent":"[quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]Noxx[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n I am debating on Black and Pink and Hot Pink and Lime Green. I think the pink and green will look better in pictures but cant decide.  \n thoughts???[\/quote] \n Hot pink and lime green may be hard to pull off for some people.  Lime green, especially, is one of those colors that doesn&#039;t flatter everyone.  Black and pink is a classy color combination.. and you could even do the hot pink with black.  Personally, I think that the hot pink will stand out marvelously in pictures.  I just have some reservations on pairing it with the lime green.  If you think your wedding party will look okay in that shade of green, then go for it. :)","Attachments":[],"Id":1649895,"PostDate":1344331371,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>Noxx<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> I am debating on Black and Pink and Hot Pink and Lime Green. I think the pink and green will look better in pictures but cant decide.\u00a0<\/p> <p> thoughts???\u00a0<\/p> <\/blockquote> <p> Hot pink and lime green may be hard to pull off for some people. \u00a0Lime green, especially, is one of those colors that doesn't flatter everyone. \u00a0Black and pink is a classy color combination.. and you could even do the hot pink with black. \u00a0Personally, I think that the hot pink will stand out marvelously in pictures. \u00a0I just have some reservations on pairing it with the lime green. \u00a0If you think your wedding party will look okay in that shade of green, then go for it. <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> \u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"bmelko@ymail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":47,"GroupName":"Site Supporter","JoinDate":1337785216,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-255751.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":173,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"bmelko","Id":255751,"Name":"bmelko","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":67485,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"6f754f75d41f85efb4eb93bf2eea81d1","RawContent":"[quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]Noxx[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n I am debating on Black and Pink and Hot Pink and Lime Green. I think the pink and green will look better in pictures but cant decide.  \n thoughts???[\/quote] \n I think the lime green and pink is HOT!! and completely different. Because they are both bold colors and pop you need to make one an accent color and one a main color with base color like yellow or orange. You can even do aqua or black as a base color.  \n \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/155912\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/155913\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/155914\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img] \n \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/155915\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img]","Attachments":[],"Id":1649914,"PostDate":1344336182,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>Noxx<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> I am debating on Black and Pink and Hot Pink and Lime Green. I think the pink and green will look better in pictures but cant decide.\u00a0<\/p> <p> thoughts???\u00a0<\/p> <\/blockquote> <p> I think the lime green and pink is HOT!! and completely different. Because they are both bold colors and pop you need to make one an accent color and one a main color with base color like yellow or orange. You can even do aqua or black as a base color.\u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p id=\"yui_3_4_1_1_1344353834674_1583\"> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' data-id=\"155912\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/155912\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p id=\"yui_3_4_1_1_1344353834674_2288\"> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' data-id=\"155913\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/155913\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p id=\"yui_3_4_1_1_1344353834674_3005\"> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' data-id=\"155914\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/155914\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p id=\"yui_3_4_1_1_1344353834674_3776\"> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' data-id=\"155915\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/155915\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><\/div><\/div>","Email":"sha4966@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":47,"GroupName":"Site Supporter","JoinDate":1312894978,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-243584.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Shay4966","Id":243584,"Name":"Shay4966","IsOnline":false}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":378,"TotalPages":38,"CurrentPage":70,"NextPage":80,"PreviousPage":60,"LastPage":370},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
