{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":67485,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"601b798de0ac58723f122cde17ffe91e","RawContent":"[quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]bmelko[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n I think it&#039;s going to look amazing.  The  teal is a good contrast against the sand.  I don&#039;t feel like they&#039;re too dark; in fact, I love the neutral colors together, the blend really well.[\/quote] \n  I second that!!.. Cinnagirl, I love your colors!.","Attachments":[],"Id":1653701,"PostDate":1345190973,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>bmelko<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> I think it's going to look amazing. \u00a0The \u00a0teal is a good contrast against the sand. \u00a0I don't feel like they're too dark; in fact, I love the neutral colors together, the blend really well.\u00a0<\/p> <\/blockquote> <p> \u00a0I second that!!.. Cinnagirl, I love your colors!.<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"britneyrasco@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1329412672,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-251499.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"MissBubbles205","Id":251499,"Name":"MissBubbles205","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":67485,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"0106691ae40ccc9d77cf89b037c79873","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; &lt;span&gt;\t Quote:&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;div class=\"quote-container\"&gt; &lt;div class=\"quote-block\"&gt; Originally Posted by &lt;strong&gt;bmelko&lt;\/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;img alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/&gt;\n &lt;p&gt; I think it&#039;s going to look amazing. &amp;nbsp;The &amp;nbsp;teal is a good contrast against the sand. &amp;nbsp;I don&#039;t feel like they&#039;re too dark; in fact, I love the neutral colors together, the blend really well.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;\/div&gt; &lt;\/div&gt; &lt;p&gt; +1 Cinnagirl. I love bold saturated colors and these will compliment the sand and the sea perfecty! I had similar reservations with my color scheme of chartreuse and sangria, but I made the chartreuse my primary and added fuchsia as an additional accent color.&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1653727,"PostDate":1345196587,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> <span>\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Quote:<\/span><\/p> <div class=\"quote-container\"> <div class=\"quote-block\"> Originally Posted by <strong>bmelko<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/><\/span><br \/> <p> I think it's going to look amazing. \u00a0The \u00a0teal is a good contrast against the sand. \u00a0I don't feel like they're too dark; in fact, I love the neutral colors together, the blend really well.\u00a0<\/p> <\/div> <\/div> <p> +1 Cinnagirl. I love bold saturated colors and these will compliment the sand and the sea perfecty! I had similar reservations with my color scheme of chartreuse and sangria, but I made the chartreuse my primary and added fuchsia as an additional accent color.<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"tapurnell@msn.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1326156151,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-249670.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"ChocoTaco7568","Id":249670,"Name":"ChocoTaco7568","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":67485,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"d6e6a3e3166930f0f348f5b8902e3e6c","RawContent":"[quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]bmelko[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n I think it&#039;s going to look amazing.  The  teal is a good contrast against the sand.  I don&#039;t feel like they&#039;re too dark; in fact, I love the neutral colors together, the blend really well.[\/quote] \n \n LOVE! Very Elegant :)","Attachments":[],"Id":1653730,"PostDate":1345196808,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>bmelko<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> I think it's going to look amazing. \u00a0The \u00a0teal is a good contrast against the sand. \u00a0I don't feel like they're too dark; in fact, I love the neutral colors together, the blend really well.\u00a0<\/p> <\/blockquote> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> LOVE! Very Elegant <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"bridemichelle@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1335696812,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-254695.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"PuntaBride","Id":254695,"Name":"PuntaBride","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":67485,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"f2ab4772b6f60a7fa30d9d0fc55fbf64","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; Thank you so much Shay4966! love the ideas you posted. I like to idea of adding orange or yellow as well.&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1653912,"PostDate":1345214364,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Thank you so much Shay4966! love the ideas you posted. I like to idea of adding orange or yellow as well.<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"a_fleetwood6@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1333230068,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-253433.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Noxx","Id":253433,"Name":"Noxx","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":67485,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"1178b1aec4bd9cbaa46e10aa33f2d585","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; Thanks ladies!! I feel much more confident about our colour scheme now. I think it&#039;s just hard when I don&#039;t see many beach weddings on the internet with deeper colour schemes so I find it hard to visualize what I&#039;m planning. But I&#039;m sure it&#039;ll all work out now. &amp;nbsp;:)&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1654376,"PostDate":1345366485,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Thanks ladies!! I feel much more confident about our colour scheme now. I think it's just hard when I don't see many beach weddings on the internet with deeper colour schemes so I find it hard to visualize what I'm planning. But I'm sure it'll all work out now. \u00a0<img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"kschnella@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1328770673,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-251197.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"cinnagirl","Id":251197,"Name":"cinnagirl","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":67485,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"4ce32d8e669131b390a63ef9d14d623c","RawContent":"[quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]bmelko[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n I think it&#039;s going to look amazing.  The  teal is a good contrast against the sand.  I don&#039;t feel like they&#039;re too dark; in fact, I love the neutral colors together, the blend really well.[\/quote] \n \n Agree - I think having some more neutral colors with a \"pop\" of something bright is stunning for a beach wedding. We&#039;re doing whites, silvers and sandy colors, and then bright orangy-pink is the pop. It&#039;s enough to belend with the sand I think, and add a tropical touch (just like your green)!","Attachments":[],"Id":1654658,"PostDate":1345466257,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>bmelko<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> I think it's going to look amazing. \u00a0The \u00a0teal is a good contrast against the sand. \u00a0I don't feel like they're too dark; in fact, I love the neutral colors together, the blend really well.\u00a0<\/p> <\/blockquote> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Agree - I think having some more neutral colors with a \"pop\" of something bright is stunning for a beach wedding. We're doing whites, silvers and sandy colors, and then bright orangy-pink is the pop. It's enough to belend with the sand I think, and add a tropical touch (just like your green)!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span><span>What: Mexican beach wedding extravaganza<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/p><span><\/span><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span><span>When: January 18, 2013<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/p><span><\/span><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span><span>Where: <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/www.realresorts.com\/The-Royal-Playa-Carmen\/\"><span>The Royal Playa Del Carmen<\/span><\/a><\/span><\/span><\/span><\/p><span><\/span><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span><span>Who: Soon-to-be Mr. & Mrs. Sprague; 50+ guests; <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/www.delsolphotography.com\/blog\"><span>del Sol Photography<\/span><\/a><\/span><\/span><\/span><\/p><span><\/span><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span><span>Check out our wedding photos sneak peek from Del Sol: <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/delsolphotography.com\/jordan-garrett-royal-playa-del-carmen-destination-wedding\/\">http:\/\/delsolphotography.com\/jordan-garrett-royal-playa-del-carmen-destinatio...<\/a><\/span><\/span><\/span><\/p><span><\/span><\/div><\/div>","Email":"jordanblakesley@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1337262132,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-255499.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"jordanb","Id":255499,"Name":"jordanb","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":67485,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"a2f085db18092c9cb2e96ad062c7c01e","RawContent":"Gorgeous, cinnagirl! I just finished a jewelry collection for a bride who will be incorporating the peacock teal in her wedding! To tie everything together, some of her jewelry and her bridesmaids jewelry (barefoot sandals, earrings, bracelet) add in those POPs! \n \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/158739\/width\/500\/height\/1000[\/img] \n \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/158740\/width\/500\/height\/1000[\/img] \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/158741\/width\/500\/height\/1000[\/img] \n [quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]cinnagirl[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n Everyone&#039;s doing such bright colours! I feel like mine are dark in comparison.  \n \n Our colours are teal with brown, beige, white and green. Keeping it fairly neutral, but I&#039;m hoping the teal will pop against the sand.  \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/158088\/width\/350\/height\/700[\/img][\/quote]","Attachments":[],"Id":1654874,"PostDate":1345502465,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Gorgeous, cinnagirl! I just finished a jewelry collection for a bride who will be incorporating the peacock teal in her wedding! To tie everything together, some of her jewelry and her bridesmaids jewelry (barefoot sandals, earrings, bracelet) add in those POPs!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p id=\"yui_3_4_1_1_1345520257648_1915\"> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"\" data-id=\"158739\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/158739\/width\/500\/height\/1000\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"\" data-id=\"158740\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/158740\/width\/500\/height\/1000\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"\" data-id=\"158741\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/158741\/width\/500\/height\/1000\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>cinnagirl<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> Everyone's doing such bright colours! I feel like mine are dark in comparison.\u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Our colours are teal with brown, beige, white and green. Keeping it fairly neutral, but I'm hoping the teal will pop against the sand.\u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p id=\"yui_3_4_1_1_1345169105507_1883\"> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"\" data-id=\"158088\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/158088\/width\/350\/height\/700\" \/><\/span><\/p> <\/blockquote>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"redibychelsea@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1245201937,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-218520.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"bondgirl0072010","Id":218520,"Name":"bondgirl0072010","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":67485,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"ca2a80352f0bae0e8a4f07e0f30a2d36","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; Can anyone help me with my colors.....&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; I had originally picked out dark purple (eggplant) with ivory lace and burlap..&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; But my groom really wants light grey linen suits and i cant picture it in my head mixing well with the burlap accents&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; So i was debating on taking out the burlap and just using ivory lace with eggplant and grey\/silver&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; But my invites and most of my wedding stationary are being done with kraft paper which is brown and rustic, which i picked out because of the burlap. The paper is already bought and i would hate for it to goto waste.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Any ideas? or is it just me that i shouldnt mix the grey with the brown?&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1654887,"PostDate":1345504470,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Can anyone help me with my colors.....<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I had originally picked out dark purple (eggplant) with ivory lace and burlap..<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> But my groom really wants light grey linen suits and i cant picture it in my head mixing well with the burlap accents<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> So i was debating on taking out the burlap and just using ivory lace with eggplant and grey\/silver<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> But my invites and most of my wedding stationary are being done with kraft paper which is brown and rustic, which i picked out because of the burlap. The paper is already bought and i would hate for it to goto waste.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Any ideas? or is it just me that i shouldnt mix the grey with the brown?<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"dazeydawl14@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"70.76.192.165","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1327958330,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-250750.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":150,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Dazeydawl","Id":250750,"Name":"Dazeydawl","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":67485,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"d03da71573a7473696c69be233cf1b24","RawContent":"[quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]bondgirl0072010[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n Gorgeous, cinnagirl! I just finished a jewelry collection for a bride who will be incorporating the peacock teal in her wedding! To tie everything together, some of her jewelry and her bridesmaids jewelry (barefoot sandals, earrings, bracelet) add in those POPs! \n \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/158739\/width\/500\/height\/1000[\/img] \n \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/158740\/width\/500\/height\/1000[\/img] \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/158741\/width\/500\/height\/1000[\/img] \n[\/quote] \n \n Those are lovely Chelsea! I&#039;ll definitely be in contact regarding some barefoot jewelry for myself and my bridal party. :)","Attachments":[],"Id":1654912,"PostDate":1345522674,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>bondgirl0072010<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> Gorgeous, cinnagirl! I just finished a jewelry collection for a bride who will be incorporating the peacock teal in her wedding! To tie everything together, some of her jewelry and her bridesmaids jewelry (barefoot sandals, earrings, bracelet) add in those POPs!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p id=\"yui_3_4_1_1_1345520257648_1915\"> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"\" data-id=\"158739\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/158739\/width\/500\/height\/1000\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"\" data-id=\"158740\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/158740\/width\/500\/height\/1000\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"\" data-id=\"158741\" data-type=\"61\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/content\/type\/61\/id\/158741\/width\/500\/height\/1000\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <\/blockquote> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Those are lovely Chelsea! I'll definitely be in contact regarding some barefoot jewelry for myself and my bridal party. <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"kschnella@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1328770673,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-251197.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"cinnagirl","Id":251197,"Name":"cinnagirl","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":67485,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"519893a96efbc0d42974814ba52a024f","RawContent":"[quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]Dazeydawl[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n Can anyone help me with my colors..... \n \n I had originally picked out dark purple (eggplant) with ivory lace and burlap.. \n \n But my groom really wants light grey linen suits and i cant picture it in my head mixing well with the burlap accents \n \n So i was debating on taking out the burlap and just using ivory lace with eggplant and grey\/silver \n \n But my invites and most of my wedding stationary are being done with kraft paper which is brown and rustic, which i picked out because of the burlap. The paper is already bought and i would hate for it to goto waste. \n \n Any ideas? or is it just me that i shouldnt mix the grey with the brown?[\/quote] \n \n Hi [b]Dazeydawl[\/b] \n In my opinion, you can change the wedding colours without the burlap and keep your wedding invites as it. Most people won&#039;t notice if the invites don&#039;t match the wedding colours. I&#039;d choose what you think will look best in photos-maybe ask your wedding photographer about adding the grey\/brown\/purple togther?","Attachments":[],"Id":1655187,"PostDate":1345575414,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>Dazeydawl<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> Can anyone help me with my colors.....<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I had originally picked out dark purple (eggplant) with ivory lace and burlap..<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> But my groom really wants light grey linen suits and i cant picture it in my head mixing well with the burlap accents<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> So i was debating on taking out the burlap and just using ivory lace with eggplant and grey\/silver<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> But my invites and most of my wedding stationary are being done with kraft paper which is brown and rustic, which i picked out because of the burlap. The paper is already bought and i would hate for it to goto waste.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Any ideas? or is it just me that i shouldnt mix the grey with the brown?<\/p> <\/blockquote> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p  style=\"margin-left: 0px\"> Hi\u00a0<strong style=\"font-style: normal; font-weight: bold; \">Dazeydawl<\/strong><\/p> <p  style=\"margin-left: 0px\"> In my opinion, you can change the wedding colours without the burlap and keep your wedding invites as it. Most people won't notice if the invites don't match the wedding colours. I'd choose what you think will look best in photos-maybe ask your wedding photographer about adding the grey\/brown\/purple togther?<\/p> \r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"bethvolpov@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":47,"GroupName":"Site Supporter","JoinDate":1313025644,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-243668.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Vancouver Bride","Id":243668,"Name":"Vancouver Bride","IsOnline":false}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":378,"TotalPages":38,"CurrentPage":90,"NextPage":100,"PreviousPage":80,"LastPage":370},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
